      "id": 1,
      "text": "Seven Springs was originally incorporated as Whitehall in 1855, honoring planter William Whitefield's 1741 home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1951 the town adopted the name Seven Springs, reflecting the local mineral springs that once drew visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, a battle took place near Seven Springs in December 1862, marking its early historical significance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town once hosted a resort that opened in 1881 to attract guests to its seven mineral springs, but it closed in 1944.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Seven Springs sits along the Neuse River, a key geographic feature of the area.",
